 "extraction": "VizieR ASU TSV export, -out=**&-out.max=unlimited. Cleaned file maps upstream columns to a standard schema (id,ra_deg,dec_deg,z,z_err,q_flag,member_flag) and appends sep_arcmin and R_proj_Mpc computed from the cluster centre with FlatLambdaCDM(H0=70,Om0=0.3). No rows dropped. Where the upstream redshift is stored as a velocity cz in km/s it is converted to z=cz/c and its uncertainty is converted consistently to dz=e_cz/c; otherwise no values are altered. Raw upstream response kept verbatim in raw/.",
 "note": "Abell 370 (z=0.375). Lagattuta, Richard, Bauer et al. 2022, MNRAS 514, 497 ('The Abell 370 Pilot-WINGS master data catalogue'). 1250 redshifts - the LARGEST and widest MUSE sample for A370 and the best single A370 catalogue in this product. Quality: column q_z, 1 (low) to 3 (high) reliability. Column IDfrom records the detection route and column Field records which MUSE data set the object came from. Instrument: VLT/MUSE mosaic (Pilot-WINGS), with HST F435W-F160W photometry attached; coordinates are aligned to the Gaia DR2 frame. Selection function: continuum-prior plus blind emission-line detection inside the MUSE mosaic footprint; not a simple magnitude limit. Sky coverage: extends to ~2.9 arcmin (~0.92 Mpc projected); 90% within ~0.70 Mpc. Still a small-field IFU mosaic - it roughly doubles the radial reach of the earlier 2019 A370 mosaic but remains restricted to the cluster core, so sigma(R) for A370 can only be resolved over sub-Mpc radii.",
